--! This module can be useful while *developing* an application. It is not
--! meant for shipping code: a release build should not be printing to the
--! console or crashing on a `todo`.
--!
--! **A `--release` build that reaches any of these three is refused**, with
--! the use sites named, so "not meant for shipping code" is a rule and not
--! only advice.
--!
--! All three declarations are `foreign`, because all three do something the
--! language itself cannot: write to the outside world, stop the program, and
--! look at a value's representation without knowing its type.

--| Print a value to the console, tagged with a label, and return it
--| unchanged. Because the value comes back out, a `log` can be dropped into
--| the middle of an expression without moving any other code.
--|
--|     total = List.sum (Debug.log "prices" prices)
--|
--| The label comes first, as in Elm: it is short and the value is often
--| long, so the label stays beside the word `log` when the call wraps an
--| expression (`language.md` §12.4). As a statement, `Debug.log "done" ()`.
pub foreign impure log : String, a → a


--| Say that some code is not done yet, with a message about what is missing.
--| It type-checks as anything at all, so the rest of the module still
--| compiles, and it crashes with the message if it is ever reached.
--|
--|     view model =
--|         Debug.todo "render the settings page"
pub foreign impure todo : String → a


--| Turn any value into a string for debugging.
--|
--|     Debug.toString [ 1, 2 ] == "[1,2]"
--|
--| The exact text is not a promise and will change. For output a user reads,
--| write the conversion yourself.
pub foreign pure toString : a → String
